cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Shishin attestation log"
message: >-
  If you reference this log, or any figure whose provenance it establishes,
  please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Shishin Research"
    website: "https://shishin.io"
abstract: >-
  A public, tamper-evident, timestamped record of the daily equity signals and
  net asset value published by Shishin Research. Each trading day is committed
  as a chained SHA-256 hash and anchored to the Bitcoin blockchain via
  OpenTimestamps at commit time, then revealed in full after a delay, so any
  third party can confirm that a published figure existed unaltered at the
  committed time. The data (chain/, reveals/) is CC BY 4.0; the included
  verifier (verify.py, standard library only) is MIT so that anyone can build
  an independent checker.
url: "https://github.com/Azoq/shishin-attestation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Azoq/shishin-attestation"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
date-released: 2026-06-27
keywords:
  - attestation
  - commit-reveal
  - opentimestamps
  - track record
  - reproducibility
  - quantitative finance
